    <main id="content" tabindex="-1">
      <h1>Who publishes this site</h1>
      <p>A reader who wants to know who is behind a project should not have to read a commit history to find out. This page is where that answer lives, and it is one page rather than a paragraph on another, because somebody looking for it looks for a page with this name.</p>
      <p>Every answer below is read out of the tree rather than written into the page, so an answer that changes is a change to one value and not an edit to prose. Where an answer has not been taken, the line says so and says what it is waiting on, rather than leaving an empty space that reads as an answer of nothing.</p>
      <p>Publishing a site under a name of one&#39;s own carries a provider identification duty in some jurisdictions. Which one applies turns on where the publisher sits and on whether a site is read as private or as commercial, and none of that is decided by anything in the tree that produces these pages. Nothing here is legal advice.</p>
      <p>What happens to a request for a page on this site is a separate question, and it has its own page rather than a summary here. A summary would be a second copy of those statements, and a second copy is what goes quietly out of step with the first.</p>
      <nav aria-label="Where to go from here">
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/privacy/">What happens to a request for a page here</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
      <dl>
        <dt>Who publishes this site</dt>
        <dd>
          Not decided yet. entry 8 of issue 7 is where that answer is taken, and this
          line says so rather than standing empty.
        </dd>
        <dt>How to reach whoever publishes it</dt>
        <dd>
          Not decided yet. entry 8 of issue 7 is where that answer is taken, and this
          line says so rather than standing empty.
        </dd>
        <dt>Whether a postal address is published</dt>
        <dd>
          Not decided yet. entry 8 of issue 7 is where that answer is taken, and this
          line says so rather than standing empty.
        </dd>
      </dl>
      
    </main>
    <footer>
